<description>&lt;p&gt;Armed clashes have erupted in Yaounde, Douala and Maroua as Cameroonian security forces confront Ambazonian separatists, extending fighting beyond the Northwest and Southwest. The conflict, which began after the 2016‑17 protest suppression, now reaches the capital and major port city, indicating a geographic expansion. Separatist attacks continue in the Anglophone regions, as noted in recent coverage of the war ten years on. The fighting remains intense, with 231 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP. This marks a shift from earlier reports that focused on isolated attacks within the Anglophone zones.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikwFBVV95cUxNQTNNdzM1YUZrbVBqY3hvNHRPdF9fMno4VE1GRlE1eGIwaEtldGdJS25zUnpPWVZ6dC1mNVVlZnYwTmNDOEt4WWd6bHVTeDVVRHVGVWg4QkVGNENCZkhkaWNVWTFGNURSZUxmRks3aVN0SXp0T0dGT2JtOVA5Rkh6X0ozMDRmY3FrdmJHakY5bWx6Rzg?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Africa Report&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Nation Newspaper&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxObTM4QUgwMkFSU1hZWlJvMGNUR1VUeUUxdmI2NlRKQ2l4ZGc3dHR5alRTdDdJUFY5ZDh4MG1RTEc3b3lwd2lhUEllNTlkNjh1bWlpNUxoMG5Fd1JoeGwwRnZwZGF1Q19WV3pZd29PQ0xXVmlnck1TWXVVZ2pkYWVyTThSSmZqbnBRN2hvYVpBZmpOcHZnZkF1amoyZzBhU0FfSzNQYnUyZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Genocide Watch&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Nation Newspaper&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxOM1JLSmlLZEZtblczbzcxaHFVZjR6ZVl6dzdIVmJ0QnlqbV8xa3dVLS1qZmI0N0stSkwxcXhNa0o1M29jYl9IWlloUjBLQVMwc2t4a1gtY1RRWUZJc3ZqLUdkaWVCajEwR3ZZS2pQdG5QYXVvOG11Y0w3VmM1VmhPUXRpc1NuOGp1a3JPdjJUSVlEeElJSDI0T2dGNkRRT1V2Vm9Yam1R?oc=5&quot;&gt;Hoodline&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google